# K114s r3a kernel: patches in the order they are applied to the running kernel's source.
#
# Base: aurora-silicon/linux a34d26c2 + betizzel/omarchy-m5 linux-j714s-27.2.patch (19 patches,
# release omarchy-j714s-3 "v272-4"), the source of the running K114S-R1 kernel, then:
#
#   0. patches/linux/pr1568.patch         `patch -Np1 --no-backup-if-mismatch` (git am refuses it: one hunk
#                                          needs fuzz); this is what the running kernel has
#   1. localversion.10-pkgrel             the file's content becomes  -17.v272-4-k114s-r3a  (no newline needed)
#                                          so the release is 7.3.0-17.v272-4-k114s-r3a-ARCH, not the
#                                          running kernel's 7.3.0-17.v272-4-ARCH
#   2. the patches below, with `git am`, in this order
#   3. configuration: the running kernel's config + patches/linux/config/k114s-r3.config, validated
#      (docs/r3-integration.md, "Kernel")
#
# Order: sleep-lid first (it carries #1688 and #1844, which r3/display-gpu also has: taken once, from here),
# then the display driver's 120 Hz gate and bindings, then sound, then USB. Every patch applies cleanly
# in this order (agent-run, git am, no fuzz).
sleep-lid/0001-PCI-apple-qualify-the-K116s-for-suspend-to-idle-over.patch
sleep-lid/0002-PCI-apple-let-devices-below-a-kernel-trained-port-le.patch
